{
  "_doc": "Each case runs on a fresh in-memory database. setup.customers: [name, ...]; setup.transactions: [customer, type, amount, currency, in_session?]. in_session=true marks it as recorded in this chat session (so undo_last can see it). expect.transactions: the exact new rows (customer, type, amount, currency); [] = nothing may be recorded. expect.undone: customers whose seeded row must end up undone. reply_has_any: at least one of these strings in the reply. Suppliers (stage 10) are written \"مورد:<name>\" in transactions and expectations. transactions_any_of: several acceptable outcomes. Withdrawals (stage 11): setup.withdrawals [amount, currency, reason, in_session?]; expect.withdrawals [amount, currency, a word the reason must contain]; expect.withdrawals_undone: how many seeded ones end up undone. Memory (stage 12): setup.memories [text]; expect.memories_added: how many new memories. Drawer (stage 15): setup.drawer_day {opening, transactions, withdrawals, close?} = an opening count after the old balances, the day's entries, then optionally a close. expect.drawer_counts_added, expect.drawer_opening (iqd), expect.drawer_cash_sales {IQD: n} of the new close, expect.from_drawer (of the last new transaction). Cash ins (stage 16): setup.drawer_day.cash_ins [amount, currency, label]; expect.cash_ins [amount, currency, a word the label must contain]. Items and sales (stage 17): base_setup.items [name, price, cost, unit]; setup.sales [item, qty, payment]; expect.sales [[payment, total, customer or null, {item: qty}]]; expect.items_added. Alerts (stage 19): setup.overdue [customer] = their entries 45 days old; setup.just_now [[name, type, amount, currency]] = recorded a minute ago; expect.recurring_added.",
